# reference.in: this family's reference requirements, resolved to the exact, hashed reference.lock
# beside this file by `python -m rcp_ndcg_test.jobs.reference_lock` (owner decision 35). The tool
# constrains torch and the CUDA stack to the engine image's freeze; every other pin installs into
# the family's reference venv and takes precedence over the image's copy. Never edit the lock by hand.
# The reference environment for recipes/qwen3-vl-reranker/reference.py, in ITS OWN python
# (--reference-python; never the harness's process, never the engine image). Install with the
# reference python: pip install -r reference.lock. The wave runner takes it via
# --reference-python; the reference subprocess runs while the engine on that slot is up and
# releases its memory when it exits.
#
# The referent is the model card's scripts/qwen3_vl_reranker.py, byte-identical at every variant's
# pinned revision (2b @ 4bd860ac, 8b @ b212dc8c; the transformers
# path): Qwen3VLForConditionalGeneration backbone + the sigmoid head built from the LM head's
# yes/no rows. render() needs the tokenizer files only (no torch); score() needs everything.
